{
  "title": "koylu_muhabbet_saruca_hatun",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "node:start",
      "type": "START",
      "position": "(0.0, 0.0)"
    },
    {
      "id": "node:selam",
      "type": "DIALOGUE",
      "position": "(350.0, 0.0)",
      "character": "Saruca Hatun",
      "text": "Come, child, sit and catch your breath. Soup simmers on the hearth, and the granary keys sway from my sash. Do you lack for anything?"
    },
    {
      "id": "node:opt_normal",
      "type": "DIALOGUE_OPTION",
      "position": "(700.0, -180.0)",
      "character": "Gatekeeper",
      "text": "Saruca Hatun, will our grain provisions carry us through the winter?"
    },
    {
      "id": "node:opt_kriz",
      "type": "DIALOGUE_OPTION",
      "position": "(700.0, 0.0)",
      "character": "Gatekeeper",
      "text": "What measures will you take if provisions grow lean?"
    },
    {
      "id": "node:opt_karar",
      "type": "DIALOGUE_OPTION",
      "position": "(700.0, 180.0)",
      "character": "Gatekeeper",
      "text": "What say you of the baker and the salt merchant we admitted through the portal?"
    },
    {
      "id": "node:rep_normal",
      "type": "DIALOGUE",
      "position": "(1050.0, -180.0)",
      "character": "Saruca Hatun",
      "text": "If we keep our accounts exact, they will suffice, child. We blend millet with wheat and bake hard biscuits from barley meal. If any man squanders grain, I chase him with my rolling pin; bounty is born of thrift."
    },
    {
      "id": "node:rep_kriz",
      "type": "DIALOGUE",
      "position": "(1050.0, 0.0)",
      "character": "Saruca Hatun",
      "text": "Beneath my granary lies a secret grain chest kept for dire emergencies, child; I open it to none, yet if our folk face starvation, I will lay it bare. Fear not; while your mother breathes, this settlement shall not starve."
    },
    {
      "id": "node:rep_karar",
      "type": "DIALOGUE",
      "position": "(1050.0, 180.0)",
      "character": "Saruca Hatun",
      "text": "The baker brought his seasoned beech kneading trough and has already stoked the tandoor; the savory scent of sourdough fills the village. The salt trader donated two sacks of rock salt to our granary. You opened the gate to worthy men; our hearth is enlivened."
    },
    {
      "id": "node:act_normal",
      "type": "ACTION",
      "position": "(1400.0, -180.0)",
      "description": "Köy Morali",
      "action_type": "SCRIPT",
      "action_script_ref": "res://src/diyalog/actions/koy_moral_action.gd",
      "values": [
        "2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "node:act_kriz",
      "type": "ACTION",
      "position": "(1400.0, 0.0)",
      "description": "Köy Morali",
      "action_type": "SCRIPT",
